      "title": "Append the next request and observation",
      "explanation": "After execution, the environment reveals $r_1^{\\mathrm{dep}}$ and successor observation $s_2^{\\mathrm{dep}}$. The updater computes $G_2=G_1-r_1^{\\mathrm{dep}}$ and appends $G_2$, while the environment transfers and appends the unchanged $s_2^{\\mathrm{dep}}$ identity. The next prompt is $(G_1,s_1^{\\mathrm{dep}},a^*_1,G_2,s_2^{\\mathrm{dep}})$, subject to the last-$K$-timestep window.",
